Policy compliance remediation is the process of correcting Azure resources that do not meet organizational requirements. Detection alone is not enough; organizations need a controlled process for bringing non-compliant resources back into compliance.

Remediation can involve:

* Adding missing tags
* Correcting configurations
* Deploying required settings
* Removing prohibited configurations
* Updating resource properties
* Requiring administrators to correct violations

For example, if a policy requires a specific tag on every storage account, remediation can help apply the required configuration to existing resources.

A real-life use case is an enterprise discovering hundreds of previously deployed resources that do not meet newly introduced governance standards.

Automated or controlled remediation reduces manual administrative effort and improves compliance consistency.
